  "title": "The Valley of Bowang",
  "place": "Bowang Slope",
  "blurb": [
    "Xiahou Dun has come south with the vanguard of Cao Cao's army, hot to run the little Liu Bei army into the ground. Liu Bei has a new adviser, three visits old, whom Guan Yu and Zhang Fei still do not quite trust. Zhuge Liang asks only for the command, a handful of seals and a valley.",
    "Bowang is a long cleft of reeds between two forested slopes, narrowing to a neck before the camp. The enemy will follow a bait down it at dusk. Zhao Yun is the bait. The wind off the northern pass turns south from the fourth round and runs straight down the valley; fire lit north of the neck will run with it. Keep the camp on bare road, and keep your own people out of the reeds when it does."
  ],
